      <div class="project-top">
        <div class="project-icon">✈️</div>
        <div class="project-links">
          <a href="https://github.com/MGK-VENKATESH/Travel_Journal" class="project-link" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="project-name">Travel Journal App</div>
      <div class="project-desc">A mobile application built with Flutter to document and manage travel experiences. Log destinations, memories, and journeys in a clean and intuitive interface.</div>
      <div class="project-stack">
        <span class="stack-tag">Flutter</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">Dart</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">Mobile App</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- PROJECT 9 — WEATHER STATE TRANSITION -->
    <div class="project-card fade-up" data-category="ml data">
      <div class="project-top">
        <div class="project-icon">🌦️</div>
        <div class="project-links">
          <a href="https://github.com/MGK-VENKATESH/Weather-State-Transition-Simulation" class="project-link" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="project-name">Weather State Transition Simulation</div>
      <div class="project-desc">A Python-based simulation modelling weather state transitions using probabilistic methods. Demonstrates how weather patterns shift between states over time using Markov Chain concepts.</div>
      <div class="project-stack">
        <span class="stack-tag">Python</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">Markov Chains</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">Probability</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">Simulation</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">NumPy</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- PROJECT 10 — COVID-19 SPREAD SIMULATION -->
    <div class="project-card fade-up" data-category="data">
      <div class="project-top">
        <div class="project-icon">🦠</div>
        <div class="project-links">
          <a href="https://github.com/MGK-VENKATESH/COVID-19-Spread-Simulation-Application" class="project-link" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="project-name">COVID-19 Spread Simulation</div>
      <div class="project-desc">A Python simulation application modelling the spread of COVID-19 across countries using time-series data. Features a Streamlit UI for visualization, simulation parameters, and summary analytics with real country datasets.</div>
      <div class="project-stack">
        <span class="stack-tag">Python</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">Streamlit</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">Simulation</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">Time-Series</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">Pandas</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">Matplotlib</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- PROJECT 11 — FAKE NEWS DETECTION NLP -->
    <div class="project-card fade-up" data-category="ml data">
      <div class="project-top">
        <div class="project-icon">📰</div>
        <div class="project-links">
          <a href="https://github.com/MGK-VENKATESH/Fake-News-Detection" class="project-link" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="project-name">Fake News Detection — NLP</div>
      <div class="project-desc">ML model detecting fake news using Multinomial Naive Bayes with TF-IDF features. Trained on 44,898 news articles achieving <strong style="color:var(--accent3)">98.67% accuracy</strong> with precision & recall both above 98% across fake and true classes.</div>
      <div class="project-stack">
        <span class="stack-tag">Python</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">Scikit-learn</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">NLP</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">TF-IDF</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">Naive Bayes</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">NLTK</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">Pandas</span>
      </div>
    </div>

   <!-- PROJECT 12 — NETFLIX DATA ANALYSIS -->
    <div class="project-card fade-up" data-category="data">
      <div class="project-top">
        <div class="project-icon">🎬</div>
        <div class="project-links">
          <a href="https://github.com/MGK-VENKATESH/COB" class="project-link" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="project-name">Netflix Data Analysis</div>
      <div class="project-desc">Exploratory data analysis on Netflix dataset uncovering trends in content distribution, genres, release years, and regional availability. Visualizes patterns and insights from Netflix's content library using Python.</div>
      <div class="project-stack">
        <span class="stack-tag">Python</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">Pandas</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">Matplotlib</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">Seaborn</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">EDA</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">Jupyter</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- PROJECT 13 — BANK CHURN PREDICTION -->
    <div class="project-card fade-up" data-category="ml data">
      <div class="project-top">
        <div class="project-icon">🏦</div>
        <div class="project-links">
          <a href="https://github.com/MGK-VENKATESH/PROJECTS-CLOUDCOMPUTING" class="project-link" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="project-name">Bank Customer Churn Prediction</div>
      <div class="project-desc">ML model predicting customer churn for ABC Bank using 10,000 customer records across 14 features. Compared multiple ML approaches with 70/30 train-test split, feature engineering, and overfitting analysis to find the best performing model.</div>
      <div class="project-stack">
        <span class="stack-tag">Python</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">Scikit-learn</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">Feature Engineering</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">Classification</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">Pandas</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">EDA</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- PROJECT 14 — CAPSULE NETWORK IMAGE CLASSIFICATION -->
    <div class="project-card fade-up" data-category="ml">
      <div class="project-top">
        <div class="project-icon">🛰️</div>
        <div class="project-links">
          <a href="https://github.com/MGK-VENKATESH/Python-Language/blob/main/Capsule%20Networks" class="project-link" target="_blank">GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="project-name">Satellite Image Classification — CapsNet</div>
      <div class="project-desc">Deep learning model using Capsule Networks (CapsNet) to classify satellite images into 4 categories — cloudy, desert, green area, and water. Trained on 5,631 images over 50 epochs with custom weighted margin loss achieving <strong style="color:var(--accent3)">63% test accuracy</strong>.</div>
      <div class="project-stack">
        <span class="stack-tag">Python</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">TensorFlow</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">Keras</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">CapsNet</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">Deep Learning</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">Image Classification</span>
        <span class="stack-tag">Scikit-learn</span>
